><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cytokines involved in CNS manifestations caused by <italic>Mycoplasma pneumoniae</italic>			</article-title><source><italic>Pediatric Neurology</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>33</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>105</fpage><lpage>109</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16087054</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shimizu</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kida</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuwano</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A dipalmitoylated lipoprotein from <italic>Mycoplasma pneumoniae</italic> activates NF-<italic>&#x003ba;</italic>B through TLR1, TLR2, and TLR6</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Immunology</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>175</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>4641</fpage><lpage>4646</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Into</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiura</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Yasuda</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Stimulation of human Toll-like receptor (TLR) 2 and TLR6 with membrane lipoproteins of <italic>Mycoplasma fermentans</italic> induces apoptotic cell death after NF-<italic>&#x003ba;</italic>B activation</article-title><source><italic>Cellular Microbiology</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>6</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>199</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14706104</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rawadi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramez</surname><given-names>V