-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Matthias</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rapid test for in vivo stability and DNA binding of mutated octamer binding proteins with &#x02018;mini-extracts&#x02019; prepared from transfected cells</article-title><source><italic>Nucleic Acids Research</italic></source><year>1989</year><volume>17</volume><issue>15</issue><fpage>6420</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2771660</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Homaidan</surname><given-names>FR</given-names></name><name><surname>Chakroun</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>El-Sabban</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regulation of nuclear factor-<italic>&#x003ba;</italic>B in intestinal epithelial cells in a cell model of inflammation</article-title><source><italic>Mediators of Inflammation</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>12</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>283</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14760934</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Renvoiz&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Biola</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pallardy</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Br&#x000e9;ard</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Apoptosis: identification of dying cells</article-title><source><italic>Cell Biology and Toxicology</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>14</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>120</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9553722</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bossy-Wetzel</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Detection of apoptosis by annexin V labeling</article-title><source><italic>Methods in Enzymology</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>322</volume><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10914001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Razin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Yogev</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Naot</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular biology and pathogenicity of mycoplasmas</article-title><source><italic>Microbiology and Molecular Biology Reviews</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>62</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>1094</fpage><lpage>1156</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9841667</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henderson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Poole</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bacterial modulins: a novel class of virulence factors which cause host tissue pathology by inducing cytokine synthesis</article-title><source><italic>Microbiological Reviews</italic></source><year>1996</year><volume>60</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>316</fpage><lpage>341</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8801436</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lauzurica</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mart&#x000ed;nez-Mart&#x000ed;nez</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Marazuela</surname><given-names>M</given-nam